CRASH-04: read a curve's type safely in the object-count pass

input_countObjects() tokenizes with strtok() and, on a curve's first line,
passes the next token to findmatch() to count shape curves. On a line with
only the curve name the token is NULL and match() dereferences it. A quoted
type ("Shape"), which the read pass accepts because getTokens() removes the
quotes, is not counted, so the Shape array is allocated with no elements and
project_validate() writes past it. Skip a missing type, and a leading quote,
before the match. A name-only line then reaches table_readCurve(), which
reports ERROR 203 (too few items).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-04_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/input.c b/src/legacy/engine/input.c
index 5a58319..d644eb5 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/input.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/input.c
@@ -401,8 +401,10 @@ int  addObject(int objType, char* id)
             Nobjects[CURVE]++;
 
             // --- check for a conduit shape curve
+            //     (the type may be missing, or quoted as getTokens allows)
             id = strtok(NULL, SEPSTR);
-            if ( findmatch(id, CurveTypeWords) == SHAPE_CURVE )
+            if ( id && *id == '"' ) id++;
+            if ( id && findmatch(id, CurveTypeWords) == SHAPE_CURVE )
                 Nobjects[SHAPE]++;
         }
         break;
